@segment 28-30 Westfall, Duskwood II & Redridge III
@start-level 28
# Added 2026-11-11 from the Questie audit (tools/questie_near.py): 90 Seasoned Wolf Kabobs (2000 XP; the flanks drop from the ravagers on the south road walk).
# Human Mage (from the Skyborne Mage route) 28-30. Same quests, order, hearth bind (Darkshire) and flights as segment 11 of the Skyborne Druid route.
# Carry-in: 57/67/157/181/240/453 (Duskwood, Westfall), 293 + 98190 (Stormwind), 472 + 98223 (segment 12),
# 1026 (Ashenvale, segment 13).
# Carry-out: 270 (Menethil), 472 (Dun Modr), 690 (Refuge Pointe), 1248 (Menethil), 98219 (Southshore),
# 98223 (Menethil), all for segment 12, and 1026 (segment 13).
# Changes from the druid source (no quest changed: it had no class quest here):
# - Opening: Teleport: Stormwind (known from level 20) instead of the Deeprun Tram from Ironforge; the tram is the
#   fallback. Nothing is skipped: the tram ride had no quest and no flight point.
# - Training: Jennea Cannon in the Wizard's Sanctum (Mage Quarter) instead of the Park. The teleport lands
#   there, so the TRAIN stop moved to the front of the Stormwind round (it was between the Cathedral and the Keep).
#   Added for the human: the level 26 mage chain. 1939 High Sorcerer Andromath and 1938 Ur's Treatise on Shadow
#   Magic are taken at the opening training stop; the book lies in the Tower of Ilgalar (Redridge 73.8, 47.6),
#   a short walk south of Lieutenant Fangore, whom this segment kills anyway. After Lakeshire the flight to
#   Darkshire becomes Teleport: Stormwind (hand in the book in the tower where the teleport lands, take 1940
#   Pristine Spider Silk) + the Stormwind -> Darkshire flight: one rune and about three minutes more. The silk
#   comes from the Carrion Recluses at the Raven Hill cemetery, where 58 is done; 1940 and 1942 are handed in at
#   the closing teleport to Stormwind. Unverified: where exactly the book stands in the tower and whether
#   Morganth (26, elite) has to be dealt with to reach it.
# - Last step before Archmage Malin: Teleport: Stormwind instead of the Darkshire -> Stormwind flight (the
#   flight is the fallback). It lands beside Malin and the mage trainers, where segment 12 starts.
#   The Darkshire -> Stormwind flight in the middle of the segment is kept: it lands next to the main gate.
# - A mage has no faster way to walk: the long runs are plain walks. Hearthstone used once (Darkshire).
# - All fight hints rewritten for a mage (the undead here cannot be polymorphed).
@carry 57,67,157,161,181,240,293,453,472,1026,98190,98209,98223
@done 56,66,124,154,177,266,292,96139,98189

# ---------- Stormwind ----------
N Cast Teleport: Stormwind | You start in Ironforge. The spell (from level 20) needs a Rune of Teleportation and lands you in the Wizard's Sanctum, the mage tower in the Mage Quarter. No rune or spell? Take the Deeprun Tram in Tinker Town: it arrives in the Dwarven District; then walk to the Mage Quarter. Already in Stormwind? Tick this
TRAIN @ Stormwind City, 49.6, 85.8 | Jennea Cannon, in the Wizard's Sanctum. Learn your level 26 and 28 spells (Cone of Cold is the level 26 one). Buy 5-10 Runes of Teleportation from a reagent vendor before you leave the city
A 1939 | Jennea Cannon: your level 26 mage quest
T 1939 | High Sorcerer Andromath, at the top of the Wizard's Sanctum
A 1938 | High Sorcerer Andromath. The book is in the Tower of Ilgalar in Redridge: later in this segment
T 98190 @ Stormwind City, 80.0, 38.5 | Across the city to Stormwind Keep. Highlord Bolvar Fordragon in the throne room (new in Forever)
A 98191 | Highlord Bolvar Fordragon
T 293 | Archbishop Benedictus, at the back of the Cathedral of Light
T 98191 | Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker, in the Cathedral (48.5,50.1)
A 98219 | Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker (new in Forever). A letter job for Southshore: keep it until segment 12
A 1274 | Thomas, the altar boy in the Cathedral
T 1274 | Bishop DeLavey, back in Stormwind Keep (80.2,44.1)
A 1241 | Bishop DeLavey
T 1241 | Jorgen, near the main gate at the Valley of Heroes (76.3,85.1)
A 1242 | Jorgen
T 1242 | Elling Trias, in the cheese shop in the Trade District (66.0,74.1)
A 1243 | Elling Trias. The note goes to Watcher Backus in Darkshire
FLY Sentinel Hill @ Stormwind City, 71.0, 72.5 | Dungar Longdrink, Trade District

# ---------- Westfall: the schoolhouse ----------
T 67 | Go south-west to Moonbrook. The Old Footlocker is inside the schoolhouse (41.5,66.7). Defias (level 15-20) are no danger now
A 68 @ Westfall, 41.5, 66.7 | The same footlocker

# ---------- Duskwood: Raven Hill ----------
T 240 | From Moonbrook go east over the river into Duskwood; Raven Hill is right behind the bridge. Jitters is in Raven Hill village (18.4,56.4)
T 453 | Jitters
A 268 | Jitters
N Watch for two new ghosts all over Duskwood: Ira Valor (in the woods) and Merrick Valor (on the roads) | New in Forever. Kill them when you see them: one drops Ira's Dagger, the other Merrick's Bow. Each item starts a quest (right-click it). Their exact spots are not in the data. No ghost found? Then skip the steps for 96137 / 96138 / 98447 in this segment
C 57 @ Duskwood, 20.0, 45.0 | The graveyard just north of Jitters (14-24,40-48): kill 15 Skeletal Fiends and 15 Skeletal Horrors (23-25). They are below your level: when two come, Frost Nova, step back and Arcane Explosion or Cone of Cold finishes them. Undead cannot be polymorphed
T 268 | Sven Yorgen, at his camp on the far west side (7.8,34.1)
A 323 | Sven Yorgen
C 323 @ Duskwood, 16.2, 35.3 | The northern part of the cemetery, around the crypts and the big mausoleum (13-20,27-41): 15 Skeletal Raiders (27-28), 3 Skeletal Healers (26-27), 3 Skeletal Warders (28-29). Kill the Healers first: Counterspell stops a heal or a Warder's bolt. Stay outside the crypts: Morbent Fel's house and the crypt depths are elite territory
A 225 | A Weathered Grave, at the north edge of the cemetery (17.7,29.1). Needs level 28
T 323 | Back to Sven Yorgen
A 269 | Sven Yorgen. For Stormwind, later in this segment
T 157 | Abercrombie, the hermit in the shack north-east of the cemetery (28.1,31.5). The ghouls around his hill (24-29) attack on sight: go around the east side
A 158 | Abercrombie

# ---------- Darkshire, first visit ----------
S Darkshire @ Duskwood, 73.9, 44.4 | Follow the main road east to Darkshire (a long walk; ravagers and spiders on the road are grey to green). Bind at the Scarlet Raven Tavern (Innkeeper Trelayne)
A 90 | Chef Grual, in the same tavern: Seasoned Wolf Kabobs. He already has the herbs: he only needs 10 Lean Wolf Flanks
T 158 | Tavernkeep Smitts, in the tavern
A 156 | Tavernkeep Smitts
T 68 | Clerk Daltry, in the town hall
A 69 | Clerk Daltry. For Goldshire, later in this segment
T 57 | Commander Althea Ebonlocke, in front of the town hall
A 58 | Commander Althea Ebonlocke. The Plague Spreaders are back at Raven Hill: last loop of this segment
T 225 | Sirra Von'Indi, in the town hall
A 227 | Sirra Von'Indi
T 227 | Commander Althea Ebonlocke. Do not take Mor'Ladim (228): he is elite
T 1243 | Watcher Backus, on the road at the north-east edge of town (74.8,44.2)
A 1244 | Watcher Backus. The Defias Docket is in the west of Duskwood: you get it on the loop below
A 173 | Calor, at the south-east edge of town (75.8,47.6)
C 173 @ Duskwood, 63.5, 50.0 | Brightwood Grove, west of Darkshire: kill 6 Nightbane Shadow Weavers (27-28, casters: Counterspell stops a Shadow Bolt). Worgen stand close together: Polymorph the second one when two come
T 173 | Calor
A 221 | Calor
C 221 @ Duskwood, 64.0, 58.0 | 12 Nightbane Dark Runners (28-29), a little further south in the same woods (60-68,39-78). They are fast melee: Frostbolt first, Frost Nova when they reach you and step back; eat and drink between pulls
T 221 | Calor
A 222 | Calor. Vile Fangs and Tainted Ones are 29-31: they wait for the last loop
C 156 @ Duskwood, 80.3, 59.3 | Tranquil Gardens Cemetery, south-east of Darkshire: Skeletal Horrors (79-82,56-62) drop the 8 Rot Blossoms. Stay out of the chapel
T 156 | Tavernkeep Smitts
A 159 | Tavernkeep Smitts: Zombie Juice for Abercrombie

# ---------- West loop: Defias camp, Abercrombie, Vul'Gol ----------
A 96137 @ Duskwood, 60.0, 60.0 | Ira's Dagger (new in Forever, drops from the ghost of Ira Valor; the arrow is only a guess). Tick or skip this when it applies
A 96138 @ Duskwood, 60.0, 60.0 | Merrick's Bow (new in Forever, drops from the ghost of Merrick Valor; the arrow is only a guess). Tick or skip this when it applies
C 96137 @ Duskwood, 52.0, 68.0 | Only with Ira's Dagger. Take the south road west out of Darkshire. Young Black Ravagers (23-24) run beside it all the way (46-61,59-77); the 7 Black Ravagers (24-25) are fewer: they roam north of Darkshire and Brightwood (49-70,26-63), so kill any you saw on the worgen steps or pick them up when you are back
C 90 @ Duskwood, 52.0, 66.0 | 10 Lean Wolf Flanks: Young Black Ravagers (23-24) beside the south road and Black Ravagers (24-25) drop them, the same wolves as the dagger quest. No dagger? Kill them anyway on this walk. They are grey to green: quick kills
C 1244 @ Duskwood, 23.9, 72.1 | Follow the south road to the Defias camp in the south-west (20-33,71-78). The Defias Docket is in the Defias Strongbox at 23.9,72.1. Night Runners, Night Blades and Enchanters (24-27) are easy now
T 159 | North through Raven Hill to Abercrombie's shack (28.1,31.5)
A 133 | Abercrombie
C 133 @ Duskwood, 23.5, 34.0 | Ghouls in the eastern half of the cemetery below his hill (18-27,26-39): Flesh Eaters, Rotted Ones, Bone Chewers, Brain Eaters and Plague Spreaders all drop Ghoul Ribs (7 needed). A mage cannot remove their disease: Frost Nova and keep them off you, eat or bandage after each fight
T 133 | Abercrombie
A 134 | Abercrombie
C 134 @ Duskwood, 33.4, 76.3 | Go back south to the Vul'Gol Ogre Mound (32-40,67-84). Abercrombie's Crate stands at 33.4,76.3. Ogres here are 25-30: pull singles from the edge
C 96138 @ Duskwood, 35.0, 73.5 | Only with Merrick's Bow: 8 Splinter Fist Warriors (29-30, at 32-37,69-80) and all 4 Splinter Fist Taskmasters (27-28, at 34-40,68-75). Warriors hit hard: Frostbolt from range, Frost Nova when one reaches you and step back; Polymorph a second one. Leave the south end of the mound alone for now: Zzarc'Vul (33) is for the last loop
T 1244 | Take the south road back east to Darkshire. Watcher Backus
T 90 | Chef Grual, in the Scarlet Raven Tavern
A 1245 @ Duskwood, 74.8, 44.2 | Watcher Backus
T 96137 | Sirra Von'Indi, town hall (only if you did Ira's Dagger)
T 96138 | Sirra Von'Indi (only if you did Merrick's Bow)
A 98447 @ Duskwood, 72.6, 47.5 | Sirra Von'Indi (new in Forever). Its text says it follows the two weapon quests; if she does not offer it, skip its steps. If you only finish the weapons on the last loop, take it then and decide whether one more Raven Hill trip is worth 2200 XP
FLY Stormwind @ Duskwood, 77.5, 44.3 | Felicia Maline, Darkshire

